# Everything here is about the BUILD CONTEXT, which is the repository root
# (see infra/docker-compose.yml: `context: ..` for all four app services).
# Docker tars the whole context and sends it to the daemon before reading the
# first line of the Dockerfile, so a directory excluded here is never
# transferred — even though `infra/Dockerfile` only ever COPYs a handful of
# paths out of it.
#
# Measured on a working checkout, the untuned context was ~730 MB, of which
# ~711 MB was `node_modules` and ~19 MB `.git`. Neither is copied. Both were
# being uploaded on every build.
#
# THE RULE FOR ADDING TO THIS FILE: exclude what the image demonstrably does
# not need, never what it might. A wrong entry here fails the build with a
# missing file, which is loud — but only if somebody runs the build, and the
# `onprem` profile is not in any `pnpm` gate. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s
# `compose` job builds the image for exactly that reason.

# ═══ NEVER ═══
# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile; a host `node_modules` also
# carries platform-specific binaries (esbuild, @swc/core, Prisma engines) that
# would be wrong for linux/amd64 if they ever leaked in.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output. `pnpm build` runs inside the image; a stale host `dist/` that
# reached it would be silently overwritten at best and shipped at worst.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.impeccable
.superpowers
.claude

# ═══ TEST AND TOOL ARTEFACTS ═══
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage
**/.vitest
.perfportal

# ═══ NOT PART OF THE APPLICATION IMAGE ═══
# The Go agent and the Gradle plugin are separate toolchains with their own
# gates and their own release artefacts; the Node image builds neither.
agent
clients
spikes
fixtures
docs
scripts
PerfPortal_Enterprise_PRD.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# The compose file and this Dockerfile are read by the daemon, not copied.
infra

# ═══ EDITOR AND OS NOISE ═══
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.log
.env
.env.*
